;; si's divergences from Chez Scheme 10.3.0 (doc/scheme/SCHEME-SURVEY.md, "As built: SM5 (write-ahead)"): the
;; classes every non-pass item of bin/si check falls into, each by design or deferred, with why and where that
;; was decided. An item is "KIND PROGRAM DETAIL" (arbace.scheme.check): crash (status differs), differs (stdout
;; differs, its first differing line), fails (a suite's test si fails and Chez passes: EXPR => RESULT), passes (a
;; test Chez fails and si passes). An item's class is the first whose :match finds it. bin/si divergences lists
;; them. Goi's format (test/goi/divergences.edn). Read with the Clojure reader.
[
 {:id :complex
  :title "complex numbers"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "SC7 (a): the tower's complex numbers are deferred; a non-real result raises &implementation-restriction, and a suite's test/approx of one (not caught by the suite's framework) ends its program"
  :decided "SC7 (a)"
  :match [#"complex numbers \(SC7\)"]}
 {:id :normalization
  :title "Unicode normalization"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "string-normalize-nf* need the decomposition and composition tables, not in Go's std (golang.org/x/text/unicode/norm, or tables dumped from Chez): SM6's (rnrs unicode)"
  :decided "§5.5, SM6"
  :match [#"^fails racket/unicode \(string-normalize-nf"]}
 {:id :r5rs-environments
  :title "(null-environment 5), (scheme-report-environment 5)"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "psyntax looks the environments up as libraries (psyntax null-environment-5) and (psyntax scheme-report-environment-5), which the bootstrap's library table (tools/psyntax/boot.ss) does not make yet: SC63"
  :decided "SC63"
  :match [#"^fails racket/r5rs \(eval .* \((null-environment|scheme-report-environment) 5\)\)"]}
 {:id :chez-conditions
  :title "Chez's own condition types"
  :kind :design
  :why "Chez adds &format, &continuation (and $&src) parts to the conditions its primitives raise; si raises R6RS's (&assertion, &who, &message, &irritants), as the report specifies"
  :decided "§5.3"
  :match [#"^differs larceny/exceptions line 1: .*&format"]}
]
